Top Processes and User Information.

Explanation:

Command - Purpose
ps aux - Displays all running processes.
--sort=-%cpu - Sorts processes by CPU usage (highest first).
head - Displays the first 10 lines by default.
whoami - Displays the current logged-in username.
$HOME - Displays the user's home directory.
pwd - Displays the current working directory.

         
Important concepts:

ps – Process status.
aux – Displays processes from all users with detailed information.
| – Pipe operator; passes the output of one command to another.
$HOME – Environment variable containing the home directory.
